today we're in the northern Danish city  of Aarhus brother is gay a side street  in the city centre is home to a  restaurant that's very popular with the  locals substance has only a few tables  so it's best to make a reservation chef  rene incident his team specialize in  danish cuisine he places great value in  featuring locally sourced produce in his  dishes  I like the most about cooking is to take  all these different kinds of raw  material things and watch them become  small elements in in dishes and each and  every one of them in place a different  part that's definitely what I enjoy the  most about isn't creating a thing I'm a  really raw thing while the team is  preparing a new dessert gooseberries  with pumpkin seeds and oak ice cream  Renee ensem goes to the forest to  collect Ramson Ramson is related to  onions chives and garlic that's why it's  popular as a condiment for sauces and  dips or just as a side dish  I picked the remnants because I want to  put the flavor in our dishes because the  the flavors and the smell is so it's  very classic for for all those or even  towns in this season in the spring time  so we want to give that feeling to our  guests today Renee Anson will use the  fresh Ramson to season a starter made up  of smoked haddock besides Ramson he also  needs cress radishes cucumbers and  pickled onions all the ingredients are  very classic Danish most of them are  used in Smallville smoke spread as well  both the smoked fish and the mayonnaise  and the radishes we try to do it a bit  different with the evil mayonnaise first  he cuts the fish into small pieces  instead of havoc you can also use other  smoked fish Renee Henson then scoops out  little cucumber balls which he prefers  to cucumber slices then he grates the  radishes and places them in cold water  to keep them fresh the pickled onions  are halved and the chef's next step is  to chop the Ramson and mix it with olive  oil in a blender for about five minutes  the remsen oil will serve as the base  for an herbal mayonnaise  the thing that's most important for me  in this kitchen is that all the all  ingredients we use is that they taste of  what they are we don't we don't try to  make a cucumber taste like a rabbit but  we like the cleanness of the products  now he prepares his starter courses to  add a crunchy note Renee inson garnishes  the plate with malt crackers  so here you go smoked haddock with the  cucumber ransoms and crunchy moles  co-opt Renee Hansen says greeting his  customers personally is an important  part of his work
 

